  <title>Customer terms</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Administration</gui><gui>Customer terms</gui></guiseq> keeps
  the payment terms a customer can be given in <link
  xref="contacts#edit">their contact</link>. A customer's terms decide the
  early payment discount in <link xref="customer_payment"/>, when an invoice
  becomes overdue for <link xref="customer_finance_charge">finance
  charges</link>, and the terms printed on their invoices.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Click <gui>New</gui>
    (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>N</key></keyseq>), or double click a term to
    change it.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Term / discount name</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose one: a <gui>Discount of</gui> some percent <gui>if paid
    within</gui> so many days, or <gui>if paid by the</gui> given day of the
    month, or <gui>Cash only</gui>, for no terms at all.</p></item>
    <item><p>Fill in the four lines of text and the <gui>Invoice date +</gui>
    days that print on the invoice, for instance the due date.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Save</gui>
    (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>S</key></keyseq>).</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Check <gui>Default</gui> on the term new contacts start with.
  <gui>Delete</gui> (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>D</key></keyseq>) deletes the
  selected term; if customers still use it, you are asked which term to move
  them to first, then click <gui>Update and Delete</gui>.</p>

</page>
